div.p:
b. it would substantially reduce the financial outlays of government for each ICA
                    by relying on commercial borrowing to enable participating ICAs to obtain
                    financing up to 100% of their negotiated financial requirements;

a) the existence of such a facility would tend to reduce the incentive for ICAs
                    to raise the appropriate amount of their own financing when the agreements are
                    negotiated;

c) an overdraft with the Bank or IMF would require changes in their respective
                    Charter and Articles of Agreement; such changes could be difficult to obtain and
                    would risk further undesirable amendments;
